<title>USA: Monarch to lay off 98 employees.</title>
<headline>Monarch to lay off 98 employees.</headline>
<dateline>SIDNEY, Ohio 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Monarch Machine Tool Co said Thursday it plans to lay off 98 employees at its Monarch Sidney division because of changing business conditions and continuing losses.</p>
<p>The layoffs are expected to begin August 19, the computer controller machine tools maker said in a statement.</p>
<p>Monarch also said that it was considering consolidating its Sidney operations with its Cortland division in New York, &quot;absent a more acceptable alternative before mid-August.&quot;</p>
<p>On April 30, Monarch reported a first quarter net loss of $0.01 a share versus a loss of $0.26 a share a year earlier.</p>
<p>((New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
